      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Pain is one of the most common reasons that patients seek medical care, and affects one-third of the population within a given year. Pain is not always \"functional\" (physiologic), but often is pathologic, or chronic. This article describes the mechanisms of pain, showing how a protective response can become altered to chronic pain state, such as chronic pelvic pain."},
